  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "20342113",
      "title": "Assigning Types",
      "lectureOrder": 497,
      "videoOrder": 439,
      "sourceHash": "9c641e5460c056219cf013c49500b95448b95f5cd49b5e141cff445a3feffb05",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.2,
          "end": 4.76,
          "en": "Thus far, we have some basic code here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.76,
          "end": 6.99,
          "en": "which works with numbers and strings.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.99,
          "end": 9.541,
          "en": "Now we wanna avoid that strings can pass in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.541,
          "end": 12.85,
          "en": "And for this in TypeScript files,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.85,
          "end": 16.49,
          "en": "we can set types, we can set types on variables,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.49,
          "end": 18.57,
          "en": "we can set types on parameters,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.57,
          "end": 20.91,
          "en": "in a bunch of other places as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.91,
          "end": 23.8,
          "en": "And here we can add types to those parameters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.8,
          "end": 25.95,
          "en": "To make it clear which kind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.95,
          "end": 29.2,
          "en": "of value will be accepted here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.2,
          "end": 31.54,
          "en": "we add a type to a parameter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.54,
          "end": 33.59,
          "en": "as well as to a variable by adding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 33.59,
          "end": 36.88,
          "en": "a colon after the variable or parameter name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 36.88,
          "end": 39.973,
          "en": "And then after we add the type we wanna use.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.05,
          "end": 43.75,
          "en": "Now TypeScript knows a bunch of Core Types",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.75,
          "end": 46.04,
          "en": "which are simply built into TypeScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.04,
          "end": 49.27,
          "en": "For example, the number type, integer numbers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 49.27,
          "end": 51,
          "en": "but also floating point numbers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 51,
          "end": 52.77,
          "en": "Also negative numbers of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 52.77,
          "end": 56.21,
          "en": "these are numbers and for those we have to number type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 56.21,
          "end": 58.72,
          "en": "we have to string type if you want some text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 58.72,
          "end": 61.26,
          "en": "with single or double quotes are also",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 61.26,
          "end": 63.86,
          "en": "with the template literal syntax with the backticks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 65,
          "end": 67.011,
          "en": "Sometimes we want true or false",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 67.011,
          "end": 68.63,
          "en": "and for that we got the Boolean type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 68.63,
          "end": 70.48,
          "en": "The Boolean type accepts just",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 70.48,
          "end": 73.61,
          "en": "these two values true or false.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 73.61,
          "end": 76.61,
          "en": "We also tend to find object types.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 76.61,
          "end": 81.01,
          "en": "To accept an object like this, for example, we dared",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 81.01,
          "end": 82.94,
          "en": "and also have the choice between accepting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 82.94,
          "end": 84.68,
          "en": "a general object type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 84.68,
          "end": 87.99,
          "en": "or if we want to specifically describe how the object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 87.99,
          "end": 90.21000000000001,
          "en": "should look like which properties it should have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 90.21000000000001,
          "end": 93.92,
          "en": "and which types those properties should then have.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 93.92,
          "end": 95.72999999999999,
          "en": "We can accept array types,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 95.72999999999999,
          "end": 98.53999999999999,
          "en": "for example, an array of numbers there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 98.53999999999999,
          "end": 101.28999999999999,
          "en": "we also can define if any content is allowed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 101.28999999999999,
          "end": 104.53999999999999,
          "en": "or if it for example, must be numbers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 104.53999999999999,
          "end": 106.85,
          "en": "And we got a bunch of other types as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 106.85,
          "end": 109.49000000000001,
          "en": "But let's stick to those basic types here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 109.49000000000001,
          "end": 111.52000000000001,
          "en": "And here, we clearly want a number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 111.52000000000001,
          "end": 115.637,
          "en": "So we just add number here, after num1,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 115.637,
          "end": 117.699,
          "en": "and after num2, it's the same colon number",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 117.699,
          "end": 121.25,
          "en": "and now something in interesting happens.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 121.25,
          "end": 126.15,
          "en": "My IDE already complains here, it basically tells me that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 126.15,
          "end": 130.29,
          "en": "the argument of type one as a string is not assignable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 130.29,
          "end": 132.34,
          "en": "to a parameter of type number,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 132.34,
          "end": 134.85,
          "en": "because a string is not a number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 134.85,
          "end": 139.169,
          "en": "If I compile this code, I also get this error here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 139.169,
          "end": 141.29,
          "en": "you'll see I get the error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 141.29,
          "end": 144.29,
          "en": "that about the same error as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 144.29,
          "end": 146.91,
          "en": "Nonetheless, it did compile the code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 146.91,
          "end": 149.89,
          "en": "You can also configure TypeScript to not compile",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 149.89,
          "end": 151.45,
          "en": "if it has such an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 151.45,
          "end": 153.6,
          "en": "The default is that it does compile.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 153.6,
          "end": 154.74,
          "en": "And here that's good,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 154.74,
          "end": 157.46,
          "en": "because that actually gives us another piece",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 157.46,
          "end": 161.75,
          "en": "of important information. In the compiled JavaScript code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 161.75,
          "end": 164.827,
          "en": "that colon number thing here is gone.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 164.827,
          "end": 166.918,
          "en": "Because as I mentioned before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 166.918,
          "end": 169.53,
          "en": "it's a pure TypeScript feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 169.53,
          "end": 171.67000000000002,
          "en": "It doesn't exist in JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 171.67000000000002,
          "end": 175.45,
          "en": "It's only there during development to give us exactly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 175.45,
          "end": 178.45,
          "en": "that error, which we see down there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 178.45,
          "end": 180.28,
          "en": "That's why we have this feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 180.28,
          "end": 182.75,
          "en": "We only need it during development,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 182.75,
          "end": 185.768,
          "en": "because it allows us to catch bugs like",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 185.768,
          "end": 188.18,
          "en": "this and get rid of such lines.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 188.18,
          "end": 190.39,
          "en": "Now, that's TypeScript in a nutshell.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 190.39,
          "end": 195.09,
          "en": "And this might sound trivial, but that's its core feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 195.09,
          "end": 199.15,
          "en": "The essence of TypeScript is that you are very clear about",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 199.15,
          "end": 201.64,
          "en": "the types of data you work with in different parts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 201.64,
          "end": 202.473,
          "en": "of your app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 202.473,
          "end": 206.743,
          "en": "And that overall leads to better code and less bugs.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
